1
00:00:00,286 --> 00:00:03,640
“Great idea, team. I'll present it to the CXO myself.”

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:06,073
Team? Riya built that deck alone.

3
00:00:06,209 --> 00:00:11,848
Malhotra sir. VP. Charming in meetings. And tomorrow, 10 a.m.: the CXO review.

4
00:00:12,031 --> 00:00:16,849
Two roads. Option A: call it out in the meeting. Drama.

5
00:00:16,937 --> 00:00:20,049
Option B: stay quiet. Again. Invisible.

6
00:00:20,232 --> 00:00:23,939
But there's a third road. It's about 2,300 years old.

7
00:00:24,170 --> 00:00:31,053
manasā cintitaṁ kāryaṁ vācā naiva prakāśayet, mantreṇa rakṣayed gūḍhaṁ kārye cāpi niyojayet (Chanakya Niti 2.7)

8
00:00:31,284 --> 00:00:41,465
Chanakya Niti 2.7: what you plan in your mind, don't broadcast it. Guard it like secret counsel, and put it to work.

9
00:00:41,696 --> 00:00:49,468
Handed over unguarded: private chat, no name. No record, no credit.

10
00:00:49,651 --> 00:00:52,093
So, Option C. One: your name on the file.

11
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:58,249
Two: before the meeting, one line, team cc'd: “Deck attached. Happy to walk through the numbers.”

12
00:00:58,290 --> 00:01:01,102
Three: when the numbers question comes, you answer it.

13
00:01:01,286 --> 00:01:06,907
No fight. No complaint. Just a record. Don't argue for credit. Timestamp it.

14
00:01:07,138 --> 00:01:10,920
Your move: send the mail before, or speak up in the meeting?
